  "scope": "Review and update the model-directed agent play workflow against current shared gameplay and UI changes. No new autonomous playthrough.",
  "decisionOwner": "model; scripts only perform transport, unique legal-action matching, arithmetic and complete recording",
  "changes": [
    "Legal map destinations pass the acquired allowDiagonalMapMovement flag to the shared Board.IsAdjacent overload. Actual movement still uses the formal map mover.",
    "Expose existing shared run_equip in event, event_result and rest, as well as map. Equipment keeps the current event/visit and does not consume healing, AP or event choices; combat and locked reforge remain excluded.",
    "crafting_plan treats canCraft as authoritative only in phase forge; outside it reports material readiness and canCraft:null instead of declaring the recipe unusable.",
    "Add tools/agent_play_client.py: explicit one-action selectors, full observations/catalogue, persist the exact request before sending, explicit same-request retry and re-observe after cached responses. Ambiguous selectors and missing rationale are rejected. No policy imports, route/skill selection or turn loops.",
    "Block run_next in the model execution tool to avoid its default seed 1. A fresh run requires separate explicit creation with a newly registered seed. Recovery and definitive rejection need the documented raw-command workflow; the tool does not automatically replace sessions or discard pending commands.",
    "Label legacy adventure demo as legacy-script-heuristic. Update guide with current IDs/localization boundaries, dynamic equipment/material budgets, conditional effects, all speed slots, current battle HP and formal settlement.",
    "OpenAPI descriptions updated to document phase-sensitive crafting, diagonal movement and equipment availability; document version 0.8.6, wire apiVersion remains 1."
